civvis-play*.log
# Runtime evolution state at the repo root only; data/evolved/ is a committed
# champion, the same arrangement as the league snapshot below.
/evolved/
# Runtime league state at the repo root only; data/league/ is a committed snapshot.
/league/
# The live mirror's north-up staging copy (tools/follow.py). Untracked and
# unignored, it left the `main` MANAGEMENT worktree dirty for as long as a game
# was running — and `civvis_collab.py start` refuses to force-update a dirty
# management worktree, so a live run disabled the repository's own task launcher
# and its five-minute synchronization service on that machine. Reproduced
# 2026-08-07: "cannot start from a synchronized origin/main: refusing to
# force-update dirty main management worktree".
/stage/
*.log
target-tools/
bin-run/
exhibition-supervisor.log
tools/__pycache__/
tools/*/__pycache__/
# beta/worker_test.py imports beta/verify.py for its browser plumbing, which
# byte-compiles it here.
beta/__pycache__/

# A published build is assembled, never committed: it is 6MB of engine plus a
# copy of the viewer, all of it reproducible from the revision it names.
/beta/dist/
/beta/verify.png
/beta/verify-*.png
# wrangler's local state, created by `beta/verify.py`'s password check.
/.wrangler/

# `tools/follow.py` writes the mirror follower's liveness here (CIVVIS_FOLLOW_STATUS
# defaults to the rig root). An untracked file in the repo root makes the tree
# dirty, and `civvis_collab.py start` refuses to open a task worktree from a
# dirty main management worktree — so the mirror running blocked new work.
/status.json
